{"key":"PerformanceWindow","text":"## PerformanceWindow\n\nThe **Performance Monitor** shows real-time FPS and memory usage with\ncolour-coded threshold bars.  Toggle it with `Ctrl+M` (`Cmd+M` on Mac).\n\n---\n\n@layout\nTitle Bar | 0.50, 0.04 | Toggle the Performance Monitor with Ctrl+M (Cmd+M on Mac) from anywhere in NOS.\nFPS Bar | 0.50, 0.18 | Rolling 60-sample FPS average updated every 500 ms. Green = >45 fps, Yellow = 20–45, Red = <20.\nMemory Bars | 0.50, 0.55 | Five memory categories: Managed Heap, Total Allocated, Total Reserved, Texture Memory, GFX Unused Reserved. Bars scale against a 512 MB cap. Blue = <50%, Yellow = 50–80%, Red = >80%. Widths animate smoothly.\nPlatform Info | 0.50, 0.92 | Shows the current platform (WebGL, Editor, etc.) and Unity version.\n\n---\n\n### Metrics\n\n#### FPS\n\nUpdates every 500 ms from a 60-sample rolling average.\n\n| Colour | Threshold |\n|---|---|\n| Green | > 45 FPS |\n| Yellow | 20 – 45 FPS |\n| Red | < 20 FPS |\n\n#### Memory\n\nMemory bars scale against a 512 MB cap. Bar colour:\n\n| Colour | Percentage of cap |\n|---|---|\n| Blue | < 50 % |\n| Yellow | 50 – 80 % |\n| Red | > 80 % |\n\nThe five memory categories are:\n\n- **Managed Heap** — C# garbage-collected heap (`GC.GetTotalMemory`)\n- **Total Allocated** — all Unity allocations\n- **Total Reserved** — pre-reserved Unity memory\n- **Texture Memory** — GPU texture memory\n- **GFX Unused Reserved** — reserved GPU memory not currently in use\n\nBar width transitions animate smoothly over 0.45 s.\n\n---\n\n### Keyboard Shortcut\n\n- `Ctrl+M` / `Cmd+M` — toggle the Performance Monitor from anywhere in NOS\n\n### Status: Stable\n### Purpose: OS\n\n---","screenshot":""}